WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Speed-squared effect. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Calculate drag change as speed changes

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: If density, Cd and area stay fixed, drag force follows speed squared. Real flow can change those other inputs.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: 20→40 m/s doubles speed, so modeled drag becomes 4×, not 2×.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Prediction and calculation

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Simplified flow picture; real values need test method and conditions.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Calculate drag change as speed changes
